{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":69049,"num_turns":2,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"bf2e9b88-9cc8-5107-98ab-5ea69fb3cc68","total_cost_usd":0.516532,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9390,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":6495,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9390,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6495,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9390,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9390},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":3872,"outputTokens":18,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.003962,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":6495,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":9390,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.51257,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\":\"actor:dependence-free-batch-i2-reviewer-fable-42\",\"reviews\":[{\"case_id\":\"case:256ce9b8dd475ee95a97\",\"verdict\":\"demonstrated_issue\",\"issue_class\":\"issue-class:repeated-authorized-independent-unit-entry-into-row-independent-procedure\",\"bounded_statement\":\"Within the supplied files for case:256ce9b8dd475ee95a97, the selected result — an exact two-sided binomial test of 18 natal-tube returns in 24 pooled trips against p0 = 0.5, reported as p = 0.022656 and significant at alpha = 0.05 — treats each of the 24 rows as an independent Bernoulli trial, even though the data description declares bee_tag (8 tagged females) as the independent unit and each female contributes 2 to 4 rows. The pooled trip-level test therefore inflates the effective sample size from 8 independent units to 24 correlated rows, and the reported significance is not supported at the declared unit level: a unit-level reanalysis (6 of 8 females with above-chance natal-return rates; exact two-sided binomial test 6/8 vs 0.5 gives p ≈ 0.289) is not significant.\",\"root_cause\":\"The workflow's build_report function computes hits = sum over all rows and n_trips = len(all rows), then calls binomtest(hits, n_trips, 0.5), pooling every provisioning trip from all 8 females into a single binomial count. The binomial test's validity requires the 24 trials to be independent, but multiple rows share the same bee_tag and the per-female tallies show strong within-female clustering (e.g., B-07 = 0/3, B-04 = 4/4), so repeated entries from the same authorized independent unit (the female bee) were fed into a row-independent procedure without any unit-level aggregation or dependence adjustment.\",\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The data description explicitly names bee_tag as the independent-unit column and defines one row as a single provisioning trip by one tagged female, with one trial equal to one row.\",\"observed_value\":\"Independent unit column: bee_tag; one row = one provisioning trip by one tagged female\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":20,\"end_line\":22,\"quoted_text\":\"One row is: one provisioning trip by one tagged female bee, scored for whether she returned to her own nest tube\\nIndependent unit column: bee_tag\\nOne trial is: one row\"}]},{\"description\":\"The data description states that most females appear in several rows of the table, i.e., repeated entries per independent unit are expected.\",\"observed_value\":\"most females appear in several lines\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":8,\"end_line\":10,\"quoted_text\":\"committing, and the air temperature at that moment. Females differed in how\\nbusy they were during the observation session, so most females appear in\\nseveral lines of the table.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The input table contains 24 data rows from only 8 distinct bee_tag values; for example, B-01 alone contributes four rows (trip_index 1 through 4).\",\"observed_value\":\"24 rows, 8 bees, 2-4 rows per bee\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":2,\"end_line\":5,\"quoted_text\":\"B-01,1,19.4,12.6,1\\nB-01,2,20.1,10.8,1\\nB-01,3,21.0,47.2,0\\nB-01,4,21.6,14.3,1\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow pools all rows across females into a single hit count and total, then runs one binomial test with n equal to the number of rows (24), not the number of independent units (8).\",\"observed_value\":\"binomtest(hits=18, n=24, p=0.5) on pooled rows\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":31,\"end_line\":35,\"quoted_text\":\"    hits = sum(int(trip[\\\"natal_tube_return\\\"]) for trip in trips)\\n    n_trips = len(trips)\\n    accuracy = hits / n_trips\\n    per_female = tally_by_female(trips)\\n    outcome = binomtest(hits, n_trips, CHANCE, alternative=\\\"two-sided\\\")\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report's procedure section states that every trip was treated as one Bernoulli trial and that the 24 trips were pooled into a single count for the binomial test.\",\"observed_value\":\"trips pooled as independent Bernoulli trials\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":13,\"end_line\":17,\"quoted_text\":\"Every provisioning trip in the table was treated as one Bernoulli trial, scored\\n1 when the female re-entered her own tube and 0 when she entered a different\\ntube. The 24 trips were pooled into a single count and compared with the chance\\nexpectation of 0.500 using an exact two-sided binomial test\\n(`scipy.stats.binomtest`, alternative \\\"two-sided\\\").\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report's selected statistical conclusion is the pooled trip-level binomial test, claimed significant at alpha = 0.05.\",\"observed_value\":\"p = 0.022656, declared significant\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":21,\"end_line\":21,\"quoted_text\":\"[selected-result] Exact two-sided binomial test of 18 natal-tube returns in 24 pooled trips against p0 = 0.500: accuracy = 0.750, p = 0.022656, significant at alpha = 0.05.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The per-female tallies show strong within-unit clustering of outcomes (B-07 with 0/3 natal returns versus B-04 with 4/4), indicating that trips from the same female are not exchangeable independent trials.\",\"observed_value\":\"per-female accuracies range 0.000 to 1.000 with extreme clustering\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":30,\"end_line\":33,\"quoted_text\":\"| B-04 | 4 | 4 | 1.000 |\\n| B-05 | 2 | 2 | 1.000 |\\n| B-06 | 3 | 3 | 1.000 |\\n| B-07 | 3 | 0 | 0.000 |\"},{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":21,\"end_line\":23,\"quoted_text\":\"B-07,1,23.5,58.7,0\\nB-07,2,23.9,64.2,0\\nB-07,3,24.2,55.1,0\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The report transparently presents per-female tallies and the range of trip counts per female (2 to 4), showing the authors surfaced the clustered structure; however, no unit-level test is performed and the selected result relies solely on the pooled trip-level binomial test, so this transparency does not remedy the dependence violation.\",\"observed_value\":\"per-female table shown but not used for inference\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":23,\"end_line\":26,\"quoted_text\":\"## Per-female tallies\\n\\n| bee_tag | trips | natal returns | accuracy |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":36,\"end_line\":36,\"quoted_text\":\"Trip counts per female range from 2 to 4.\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I attempted to defend the report in three ways. (1) Arithmetic check: recomputing the pooled test from the CSV confirms 18 natal returns in 24 rows and an exact two-sided binomial p ≈ 0.02266 versus p0 = 0.5, so the report accurately describes what the workflow computed — the issue is not a coding or reporting error. (2) Independence defense: I considered whether trips within a female could plausibly be treated as independent trials despite the description naming bee_tag as the independent unit. The observed data contradict this: outcomes cluster strongly within females (B-07 is 0/3, five females are 100%, B-04 is 4/4), which is the pattern expected under within-unit correlation, and the description itself flags repeated rows per female. (3) Robustness defense: I checked whether the significance claim would survive a unit-level analysis. Collapsing each female to whether her natal-return rate exceeds chance gives 6 of 8 females above 0.5; an exact two-sided binomial test of 6/8 versus 0.5 yields p ≈ 0.289, not significant, and with only 8 independent units no binary summary could reach the pooled test's precision. All three defenses fail, so the demonstrated-issue verdict stands.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"}]}","structured_output":{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-i2-reviewer-fable-42","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:256ce9b8dd475ee95a97","verdict":"demonstrated_issue","issue_class":"issue-class:repeated-authorized-independent-unit-entry-into-row-independent-procedure","bounded_statement":"Within the supplied files for case:256ce9b8dd475ee95a97, the selected result — an exact two-sided binomial test of 18 natal-tube returns in 24 pooled trips against p0 = 0.5, reported as p = 0.022656 and significant at alpha = 0.05 — treats each of the 24 rows as an independent Bernoulli trial, even though the data description declares bee_tag (8 tagged females) as the independent unit and each female contributes 2 to 4 rows. The pooled trip-level test therefore inflates the effective sample size from 8 independent units to 24 correlated rows, and the reported significance is not supported at the declared unit level: a unit-level reanalysis (6 of 8 females with above-chance natal-return rates; exact two-sided binomial test 6/8 vs 0.5 gives p ≈ 0.289) is not significant.","root_cause":"The workflow's build_report function computes hits = sum over all rows and n_trips = len(all rows), then calls binomtest(hits, n_trips, 0.5), pooling every provisioning trip from all 8 females into a single binomial count. The binomial test's validity requires the 24 trials to be independent, but multiple rows share the same bee_tag and the per-female tallies show strong within-female clustering (e.g., B-07 = 0/3, B-04 = 4/4), so repeated entries from the same authorized independent unit (the female bee) were fed into a row-independent procedure without any unit-level aggregation or dependence adjustment.","evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The data description explicitly names bee_tag as the independent-unit column and defines one row as a single provisioning trip by one tagged female, with one trial equal to one row.","observed_value":"Independent unit column: bee_tag; one row = one provisioning trip by one tagged female","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":20,"end_line":22,"quoted_text":"One row is: one provisioning trip by one tagged female bee, scored for whether she returned to her own nest tube\nIndependent unit column: bee_tag\nOne trial is: one row"}]},{"description":"The data description states that most females appear in several rows of the table, i.e., repeated entries per independent unit are expected.","observed_value":"most females appear in several lines","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":8,"end_line":10,"quoted_text":"committing, and the air temperature at that moment. Females differed in how\nbusy they were during the observation session, so most females appear in\nseveral lines of the table."}]},{"description":"The input table contains 24 data rows from only 8 distinct bee_tag values; for example, B-01 alone contributes four rows (trip_index 1 through 4).","observed_value":"24 rows, 8 bees, 2-4 rows per bee","source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":2,"end_line":5,"quoted_text":"B-01,1,19.4,12.6,1\nB-01,2,20.1,10.8,1\nB-01,3,21.0,47.2,0\nB-01,4,21.6,14.3,1"}]},{"description":"The workflow pools all rows across females into a single hit count and total, then runs one binomial test with n equal to the number of rows (24), not the number of independent units (8).","observed_value":"binomtest(hits=18, n=24, p=0.5) on pooled rows","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":31,"end_line":35,"quoted_text":"    hits = sum(int(trip[\"natal_tube_return\"]) for trip in trips)\n    n_trips = len(trips)\n    accuracy = hits / n_trips\n    per_female = tally_by_female(trips)\n    outcome = binomtest(hits, n_trips, CHANCE, alternative=\"two-sided\")"}]},{"description":"The report's procedure section states that every trip was treated as one Bernoulli trial and that the 24 trips were pooled into a single count for the binomial test.","observed_value":"trips pooled as independent Bernoulli trials","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":13,"end_line":17,"quoted_text":"Every provisioning trip in the table was treated as one Bernoulli trial, scored\n1 when the female re-entered her own tube and 0 when she entered a different\ntube. The 24 trips were pooled into a single count and compared with the chance\nexpectation of 0.500 using an exact two-sided binomial test\n(`scipy.stats.binomtest`, alternative \"two-sided\")."}]},{"description":"The report's selected statistical conclusion is the pooled trip-level binomial test, claimed significant at alpha = 0.05.","observed_value":"p = 0.022656, declared significant","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":21,"end_line":21,"quoted_text":"[selected-result] Exact two-sided binomial test of 18 natal-tube returns in 24 pooled trips against p0 = 0.500: accuracy = 0.750, p = 0.022656, significant at alpha = 0.05."}]},{"description":"The per-female tallies show strong within-unit clustering of outcomes (B-07 with 0/3 natal returns versus B-04 with 4/4), indicating that trips from the same female are not exchangeable independent trials.","observed_value":"per-female accuracies range 0.000 to 1.000 with extreme clustering","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":30,"end_line":33,"quoted_text":"| B-04 | 4 | 4 | 1.000 |\n| B-05 | 2 | 2 | 1.000 |\n| B-06 | 3 | 3 | 1.000 |\n| B-07 | 3 | 0 | 0.000 |"},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":21,"end_line":23,"quoted_text":"B-07,1,23.5,58.7,0\nB-07,2,23.9,64.2,0\nB-07,3,24.2,55.1,0"}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"The report transparently presents per-female tallies and the range of trip counts per female (2 to 4), showing the authors surfaced the clustered structure; however, no unit-level test is performed and the selected result relies solely on the pooled trip-level binomial test, so this transparency does not remedy the dependence violation.","observed_value":"per-female table shown but not used for inference","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":23,"end_line":26,"quoted_text":"## Per-female tallies\n\n| bee_tag | trips | natal returns | accuracy |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |"},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":36,"end_line":36,"quoted_text":"Trip counts per female range from 2 to 4."}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I attempted to defend the report in three ways. (1) Arithmetic check: recomputing the pooled test from the CSV confirms 18 natal returns in 24 rows and an exact two-sided binomial p ≈ 0.02266 versus p0 = 0.5, so the report accurately describes what the workflow computed — the issue is not a coding or reporting error. (2) Independence defense: I considered whether trips within a female could plausibly be treated as independent trials despite the description naming bee_tag as the independent unit. The observed data contradict this: outcomes cluster strongly within females (B-07 is 0/3, five females are 100%, B-04 is 4/4), which is the pattern expected under within-unit correlation, and the description itself flags repeated rows per female. (3) Robustness defense: I checked whether the significance claim would survive a unit-level analysis. Collapsing each female to whether her natal-return rate exceeds chance gives 6 of 8 females above 0.5; an exact two-sided binomial test of 6/8 versus 0.5 yields p ≈ 0.289, not significant, and with only 8 independent units no binary summary could reach the pooled test's precision. All three defenses fail, so the demonstrated-issue verdict stands.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]},"ttft_ms":31183,"ttft_stream_ms":2715,"time_to_request_ms":14,"type":"result","duration_ms":69592,"uuid":"d0641a8f-4c94-4542-8541-5df2bb7b1823"}
